<title>USA: PG&amp;E Diablo Canyon 2 reduced to 82 pct.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Diablo Canyon 2 reduced to 82 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production at Pacific Gas and Electric Co's Diablo Canyon 2 nuclear power unit has been cut to 82 percent of its 1,073 megawatt (MW) capacity, Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Monday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Avila Beach, Calif., was operating at reduced power for &quot;load follow,&quot; the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>Diablo Canyon 1, with a generating capacity of 1,087 MW, continues to operate at full power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
